<title>JAPAN: Japan govt says to end probe into Chinese cotton.</title>
<headline>Japan govt says to end probe into Chinese cotton.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of International Trade and Industry said on Wednesday that it would close an investigation into imports of Chinese cotton cloth, launched in August following requests from the local textile industry.</p>
<p>The Japan Spinners' Association had said Chinese cotton cloth accounts for 90 percent of total imports and 60 percent of domestic demand, and asked the ministry to take appropriate measures to restrict imports.</p>
<p>&quot;Since the Chinese side told us they would tighten measures to stabilise cotton exports to Japan, we decided to close the probe,&quot; the Trade Ministry said in a statement.</p>
</text>
